{"type":"text","timestamp":1793604193142,"sessionID":"ses_e64dcf9c0ffeYsVPcXRGq1p95F","part":{"id":"prt_19b23c55d0016XU3J6ltZUxqPN_text-0","sessionID":"ses_e64dcf9c0ffeYsVPcXRGq1p95F","messageID":"msg_19b23c55d0016XU3J6ltZUxqPN","type":"text","text":"Done. Findings and how I know:\n\n## Crash cause (fixed in `Source/PixelArena/ArenaGameMode.h`)\n`ScoreTracker` was a `UObject` created via `NewObject` but stored in a raw, non-`UPROPERTY()` pointer. Unreal's GC therefore has no reference to it and collects it. The shipped log shows the exact sequence: a garbage collection purging 412 objects at 21:05:13, then a goal at 21:05:27, then `EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION reading 0xffffffffffffffff` in `UArenaScoreTracker::AddPoints()` called from `AArenaGameMode::OnGoalScored()`. That \"crashes after a minute\" is simply how long it takes for a GC pass plus the first goal. Fix: `UPROPERTY() TObjectPtr<UArenaScoreTracker>` so the GC root keeps it alive. `Stats` was left alone — it's plain C++ freed in `EndPlay`, which is correct as-is.\n\n## No-colors cause (fixed in `Config/DefaultGame.ini`)\nThe log's `LogStreaming: Error: Couldn't find file for package /Game/Data/Palettes/DA_Primary` followed by `Palette is null, using fallback gray` shows the palette asset simply isn't in the package. The packaging settings cooked only `/Game/Maps/Arena` and `/Game/Data/Effects` — the `Palettes` directory was never cooked, so it exists only in the editor's content folder. Fix: added `+DirectoriesToAlwaysCook=(Path=\"/Game/Data/Palettes\")`.\n\n**Assumptions stated:** the absent `ArenaScoreTracker.cpp` (line 18 in the stack trace) isn't in the workspace, so I fixed the root cause visible here — the un-rooted UObject pointer — rather than guessing at code inside `AddPoints`; the crash address `0xffffffffffffffff` is consistent with GC-poisoned memory on a collected UObject. Both fixes are source/config only; no build was run since no engine exists here. Results recorded in `result.json`.","time